+# Workspace image watermark
+
+Local implementation on `codex/watermark`; no push, database application,
+deployment or app server execution. This is a Settings parity slice, not full
+legacy per-channel watermark migration or completion of the rebuild.
+
+Settings owns `src/modules/settings/watermark/`. Thin page/operations routes live
+at `/settings/watermark` and `/settings/watermark/operations`. Workspace policies
+links to the screen. English/French follows request language. Shared Button,
+FormValidation and useConfirm supply controls, associated errors and
+confirmation. Failures retain dialog and entered values for retry.
+
+Managers upload a still PNG/JPEG logo and choose a corner or center, opacity
+(0–1) and scale (0.01–1). Scale fits the logo inside that fraction of both image
+dimensions. Option updates can retain the logo; removing settings keeps existing
+copies. Missing configuration is an empty state; failed reads say Not available.
+
+Saving settings never transforms images. A person chooses an uploaded image or
+existing workspace image ID and explicitly applies the watermark. The service
+calls the provider-neutral shared raster pipeline at
+`modules/publishing/server/media/watermark.ts`, then writes a new UUID PNG using
+the existing media store. The returned media reference can be attached through
+existing authoring and appears in the image library. Originals are never
+overwritten. EXIF orientation is applied before measuring; logo alpha is
+multiplied by opacity; derived PNG metadata is stripped. Other formats are
+refused rather than flattened. There is no automatic publish-time application.
+
+UI, HTTP and MCP share `readWatermark` / `changeWatermark`. Each call reloads
+identity, membership, entitlements and permissions, checks suspension/purge,
+locks workspace/actor rows, and rechecks authority. Configuration requires current
+owner/admin Settings Workspace access. Applying requires Publishing Posts write
+and Media read access. Branding/media are workspace-wide: channel-scoped members
+and resource-restricted credentials are refused, including independent key
+restrictions. Image reads always use the actor's workspace. Mutation and
+content-free audit commit together. On failure, cleanup attempts to remove a
+new unused derivative; existing orphan cleanup is the fallback. No provider rules
+are added to shared code.
+
+MCP tools: `get_workspace_watermark`, `save_workspace_watermark`,
+`remove_workspace_watermark`, `apply_image_watermark`. Exact confirmations:
+`SAVE WATERMARK`, `REMOVE WATERMARK`, `APPLY WATERMARK`. All are declared as
+workspace tools, unavailable to restricted credentials. HTTP writes require
+same-origin requests, stream-bound bodies and strict service schemas. Responses
+are no-store; caller-selected workspace IDs are refused.
+
+Root key: `settings.watermarkMaxLogoBytes` in the owning watermark `config.ts`,
+merged through Settings. It limits uploaded/normalized logos and the HTTP body.
+Existing media upload MIME/byte, inspection pixel and Settings transaction limits
+remain active. The central registry is unchanged; release coordination must
+handle its schema-version policy.
+
+Migration: `prisma/migrations/20261030120000_rebuild_workspace_watermark/migration.sql`
+adds normalized logo bytes/settings with a workspace FK and existing purge gate.
+No generated-client changes. Workspace deletion cascades the row; shared
+FK-discovered export/erasure can discover it. Actual database byte coverage is
+unverified. Legacy per-channel watermark JSON is untouched and not imported.
+
+Evidence: 108 tests passed across 11 focused files, including service authority,
+HTTP/MCP dispatch, DOM confirmation/failure/retry, localized markup, actual Sharp
+pixel/orientation/alpha checks, storage, workspace policy, channel profiles,
+data control, MCP scope and the raw SQL void guard. TypeScript passed with
+`npx tsc --noEmit -p .`. These are synthetic automated checks.
+
+Full suite attempted and interrupted after sandbox-blocked loopback socket tests
+and an unchanged stale Analytics manifest expectation (missing Ads/Posts routes).
+Both failures reproduce alone. No full-suite/build pass is claimed. Before
+release: CUTOVER.md migration rehearsal/application, actual database concurrency
+and export/erasure, browser themes/viewports/keyboard, real MCP transport and
+attaching/publishing the copy through live-provider workflows. An unconfirmed
+retry may create another independent copy; review the image library before retry.
